.TH SITU-WALK 1 "" "situ" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
situ-walk \- read bytes against a packed situ layout image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B situ-walk
.I image
.I hex
.RB [ \-\-prefix
.IR hex ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B situ-walk
answers questions about bytes from a packed layout image, as written by
.BR "situc pack" ,
rather than from generated code: every struct, and every member of it it
can read, with the verdict validation gives. It is the same questions the
four generated backends answer, from a table, so that a disagreement
between them is a finding.
.PP
.I hex
is the message, written as hex digits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " hex"
A pseudo-header a
.B prefix(...)
checksum is summed over first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR situc (1),
.BR situ\-edit (1)
